WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.495 --> 00:00:14.775
pleaded with Wendy to come with him to Neverland.

2
00:00:14.795 --> 00:00:20.037
"I'll teach you to fly, and then we can fly there together," he said.

3
00:00:20.057 --> 00:00:22.418
"There are mermaids there too!

4
00:00:22.778 --> 00:00:24.158
Have you ever seen a mermaid?"

5
00:00:24.178 --> 00:00:27.599
"Mermaids!" cried Wendy.

6
00:00:29.019 --> 00:00:34.954
She was very excited about going, but she was worried about leaving the rest of her family.

7
00:00:34.974 --> 00:00:40.639
"You can tell the Lost Boys and me lots of stories," begged Peter.

8
00:00:40.659 --> 00:00:43.341
"Then you can tuck us into bed at night.

9
00:00:44.262 --> 00:00:46.423
None of us has ever been tucked in before.

10
00:00:47.404 --> 00:00:49.666
You can sew and make pockets for us.

11
00:00:50.507 --> 00:00:53.169
You see, none of our clothing has any pockets.

12
00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:57.032
We really could use a girl in Neverland, Wendy."

13
00:00:58.593 --> 00:01:01.856
Wendy loved the idea of taking care of Peter and his Lost Boys.

14
00:01:02.860 --> 00:01:05.642
Bravely, she tried to give him a kiss on his cheek again.

15
00:01:06.543 --> 00:01:09.945
But when she bent over to kiss him, she suddenly screamed with pain.

16
00:01:09.965 --> 00:01:14.528
"It feels as if someone is pinching me," she cried.

17
00:01:14.548 --> 00:01:18.031
"That must be Tink," said Peter.

18
00:01:18.051 --> 00:01:22.153
"I never saw her act so naughtily with a stranger before."

19
00:01:23.194 --> 00:01:24.835
Tinker Bell darted around the room.

20
00:01:24.855 --> 00:01:31.160
"She says she will pinch you again each time you do that," Peter said.

21
00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:34.802
He could not understand why, but Wendy understood.

22
00:01:35.783 --> 00:01:37.004
Tinker Bell was jealous!

23
00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:39.505
Wendy changed the subject.

24
00:01:39.525 --> 00:01:42.547
"Can you teach John and Michael to fly, too?"

25
00:01:42.567 --> 00:01:45.429
"If you like," Peter answered.

26
00:01:46.270 --> 00:01:49.592
For Wendy's sake, he was willing to put up with her brothers.

27
00:01:51.073 --> 00:01:53.995
Wendy shook her brothers, who were still asleep in their beds.

28
00:01:55.096 --> 00:01:55.896
"Wake up, John!

29
00:01:56.257 --> 00:01:57.197
Wake up, Michael!

30
00:01:57.598 --> 00:02:00.840
Peter is here, and he is going to teach us to fly."

31
00:02:01.792 --> 00:02:03.493
The boys got up, excited.

32
00:02:03.513 --> 00:02:06.375
"Can Peter really fly?"

33
00:02:07.035 --> 00:02:10.497
John asked, as he put on the black top hat he liked to wear.

34
00:02:11.557 --> 00:02:12.758
Peter didn't say anything.

35
00:02:13.378 --> 00:02:15.479
He just flew around the room gracefully.

36
00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:17.741
It looked so easy.

37
00:02:17.761 --> 00:02:19.882
"How do you do it?"

38
00:02:20.582 --> 00:02:21.182
asked John.

39
00:02:22.043 --> 00:02:24.464
He jumped off the bed and landed on his backside.

40
00:02:24.484 --> 00:02:31.328
"You just think wonderful thoughts," Peter explained, "and they lift you up in the air."

41
00:02:32.396 --> 00:02:37.138
But what Peter didn't say was that people can't fly unless fairy dust has been blown on them.

42
00:02:37.978 --> 00:02:41.880
Fortunately, Peter still had some fairy dust on his hands from Tinker Bell.

43
00:02:43.601 --> 00:02:46.122
He blew some magic dust on each of the children.

44
00:02:46.142 --> 00:02:51.784
"Just wiggle your shoulders and think lovely thoughts," he instructed.

45
00:02:52.845 --> 00:02:56.386
Michael was first, and immediately he floated up in the air.

46
00:02:56.406 --> 00:02:59.487
"Look at me, I'm flying!"

47
00:03:00.128 --> 00:03:00.648
he shouted.

48
00:03:01.864 --> 00:03:03.425
Then John and Wendy tried it.

49
00:03:04.586 --> 00:03:08.729
They were not as graceful as Peter, but each was able to fly across the room.

50
00:03:09.770 --> 00:03:11.531
Their heads bobbed against the ceiling.

51
00:03:12.712 --> 00:03:15.574
John had to hold onto his hat to keep it from being knocked off.

52
00:03:16.634 --> 00:03:18.896
Up and down they went, and round and round.

53
00:03:18.916 --> 00:03:24.079
"With a little more practice, you'll be able to fly with me to Neverland.

54
00:03:25.540 --> 00:03:28.082
You'll see the pirates and wild animals!"

55
00:03:28.923 --> 00:03:30.624
said Peter, tempting the boys.

56
00:03:31.776 --> 00:03:34.858
"Hooray—pirates!" cried John.

57
00:03:34.878 --> 00:03:37.840
"Hooray—wild animals!"

58
00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:39.280
shouted Michael.

59
00:03:42.963 --> 00:03:46.845
Meanwhile Nana, who was tied up in the backyard, kept barking.

60
00:03:48.226 --> 00:03:51.427
Liza, the servant, was preparing pudding in the kitchen.

61
00:03:52.568 --> 00:03:56.310
She was getting very annoyed; Nana had been barking all night.

62
00:03:57.291 --> 00:03:59.112
Liza stepped outside to check on her.

63
00:04:00.444 --> 00:04:07.049
"If you don't stop barking, I will have to fetch the master and mistress at Number 27," scolded

64
00:04:07.129 --> 00:04:11.092
Liza. "I'll bring them home from the party to punish you."

65
00:04:12.513 --> 00:04:14.054
This gave Nana an idea.

66
00:04:14.554 --> 00:04:16.195
She would get the Darlings herself!

67
00:04:17.476 --> 00:04:19.358
The dog quieted down on purpose.

68
00:04:21.219 --> 00:04:25.502
Then, when Liza returned to the kitchen, Nana pulled at her chain hard.

69
00:04:26.863 --> 00:04:28.064
It broke in two.

70
00:04:29.964 --> 00:04:34.627
She burst out of the yard, crossed the street, and ran into Number 27.

71
00:04:36.088 --> 00:04:39.110
Once she was inside, she waved her paws in the air.

72
00:04:40.291 --> 00:04:40.551
Now Mr.

73
00:04:40.931 --> 00:04:41.312
and Mrs.

74
00:04:41.332 --> 00:04:44.314
Darling knew that something terrible was happening at their house.

75
00:04:46.195 --> 00:04:49.797
Without saying good-bye to their hostess, they rushed into the street.

76
00:04:51.118 --> 00:04:55.661
When they reached their house, they looked up and saw the nursery's open window.

77
00:04:57.002 --> 00:04:57.883
By the time Mr.

78
00:04:57.903 --> 00:04:58.243
and Mrs.

79
00:04:58.283 --> 00:05:06.336
Darling ran up to the nursery, the children—Wendy, John, and Michael—had flown away with Peter.
